{title: 540 - Gentle Jesus, Meek and Mild}
{subtitle: SDA Hymnal #540 • GENTLE JESUS • 7s}
{lyricist: Charles Wesley}
{composer: Martin Shaw}
{key: F}
{time: 4/4}
{tempo: Moderato}
{meta: hymn_number 540}
{meta: tune GENTLE JESUS}
{meta: meter 7s}
{meta: category Christian Life - }

{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
[F/C]Gentle [C7]Jesus, meek [F/C]and [C]mild,
[F/C]Look [C7]upon [Bdim]alittle [Dm/A]child;
[Dm/A]Pity my simplicity,
[F/C]Suffer [Am]me [Dm]to [F/C]come [Gm]to [Dm/A]Thee.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
[F/C]Lamb [C7]of God, [F/C]I [C7]look [F/C]to [C]Thee;
[F/C]Thou [C7]shalt my [Bdim]example [Dm/A]be;
[Dm/A]Thou [Am]art [Dm/F]gentle, [Gm]meek, [F]and [Edim]mild,
[F/C]Thou [Bb]wast [Am]once [Dm]a [F/C]little [Dm/A]child.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
[F/C]Fain [C7]I would [F/C]be [C7]as [F/C]Thou [C]art;
[F/C]Give [C7]me Thy [Bdim]obedient [Dm/A]heart;
[Dm/A]Thou [Am]art [Dm/F]pitiful [F]and [Edim]kind,
[F/C]Let [Bb]me [Am]have [Dm]Thy [F/C]loving [Dm/A]mind.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 4}
[F/C]I [C7]shall then [F/C]show [C7]forth [F/C]Thy [C]praise,
[F/C]Serve [C7]Thee all [Bdim]my [F/C]happy [Dm/A]days;
[Dm/A]Then [Am]the [Dm/F]world shall [Gm]always [Edim]see
[F/C]Christ, [Bb]the [Am]Holy [F/C]Child, [Gm]in [Dm/A]me.
{end_of_verse}
